ef":"/en/tip/16-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Don’t stop proper treatment to try folk remedies or supplements"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/16-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"For patients with stable chronic conditions, community clinics can issue up to 12 weeks’ worth of medication at one time"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/16-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Before signing up for a family doctor in your community, find out which services are covered by yibao and which you’ll have to pay for out of pocket"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/16-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Get a dilated eye exam right after a diabetes diagnosis, then follow your doctor’s recommended schedule; check your feet once a year"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/16-08","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"People who have had kidney stones should drink 2.5–3 liters of water daily and keep salt intake under 6 grams"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/16-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Long‑term use of uric‑acid‑lowering drugs after a gout diagnosis to keep levels below 360 µmol/L"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/16"},"children":["Chapter 16"," ·"," ","How to live after being diagnosed with a chronic disease"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"16-08"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["08"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["People who have had kidney stones should drink 2.5–3 liters of water daily and keep salt intake under 6 grams"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["Roughly one in four people who have had a kidney stone will develop another one within five years. In a study of 199 people who had just experienced their first calcium stone episode, one group was instructed to drink enough water every day. Over five years, 12% of this group had a recurrence, compared to 27% of the control group that received no special instructions. UK guidelines recommend drinking 2.5–3 liters of water daily while keeping salt intake under 6 grams. Exactly 99 participants took part in this trial."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no cost at all. Simply make drinking water a dail…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["This is a five-year randomized controlled trial involving 199 patients with idiopathic calcium stones — meanin…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: People who have had kidney stones should drink 2.5–3 liters of water daily and keep salt intake under 6 grams"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no cost at all. Simply make drinking water a daily habit. On days when you sweat a lot, you’ll need even more water — the hard part is remembering to do this every day."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["This is a five-year randomized controlled trial involving 199 patients with idiopathic calcium stones — meaning no underlying cause could be identified. Participants were split into two groups: one group drank at least 2 liters of water daily, while the other received no special intervention. After five years, 12.1% of the water-drinking group had a recurrence, versus 27.0% in the control group (P=0.008). A lower P value indicates a less likely chance that this difference occurred by random chance. The average time to recurrence was 38.7±13.2 months for the water group versus 25.1±16.4 months for the control group (P=0.016). Baseline 24-hour urine volume measurements showed that stone patients produced significantly less urine than healthy individuals: men produced 1,057±238 mL versus 1,401±562 mL in healthy men (P<0.0001), and women produced 990±230 mL versus 1,239±440 mL (P<0.001). NICE guideline NG118, section 1.8.1, offers several recommendations: adults should drink 2.5–3 liters daily, while children and teens should drink 1–2 liters based on age. Adding fresh lemon juice to water is encouraged, and carbonated drinks should be avoided. Adults must also keep daily salt intake under 6 grams."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["Borghi L, Meschi T, Amato F, Briganti A, Novarini A, Giannini A (1996). Urinary volume, water and recurrences in idiopathic calcium nephrolithiasis: a 5-year randomized prospective study. The Journal of Urology, 155(3), 839-843. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0022-5347(01)66321-3","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1016/s0022-5347(01)66321-3"]},"；National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (2019). Renal and ureteric stones: assessment and management. NICE guideline NG118，第 1.8.1 条. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng118/chapter/Recommendations","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng118/chapter/Recommendations"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0022-5347(01)66321-3","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["This measure reduces recurrence rates by roughly 55% at zero cost, making it the most cost-effective recommendation in this section according to our ranking criteria. The key metric to monitor is 24-hour urine volume, which should reach at least 2–2.5 liters — not simply the amount of water you drink. People who sweat heavily or work in hot environments need to drink even more. This trial involved only patients experiencing their first idiopathic calcium stone episode; different types of stones — such as uric acid, infection-related, or cystine stones — require different treatment approaches. Anyone with a history of kidney stones should undergo a stone composition analysis and a 24-hour urine test to determine whether medication is needed. Do not cut calcium intake to prevent stones; see section 6, item 21 for more details. Severe flank or abdominal pain during a stone episode requires immediate medical attention — drinking more water alone will not resolve it. Non-painful blood in the urine may indicate other conditions; see section 1, item 27 for further information. 〔100〕 〔100〕"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":